r10.22b: phone web module MVP - the metapass side of the LAN install

install-slot/phone-install.js is the first remotely-loaded install module,
served by the Worker at GET /phone-install.js (CORS *, no-store) and loaded
by the device boot page (URL moved off the reserved loader.v1.js name).
Single-file module with a built-in pure-JS SHA-256 (crypto.subtle is
unavailable on the device's plain-HTTP origin), cross-checked against
node:crypto on 9 vectors.

Flow per design doc sections 5/6: market search through /api/plays with q,
detail metadata normalization with the no-firmware-fields = uninstallable
gate; integrated preflight (analyze, merged-image download via the
/api/firmware whitelist, store SHA-256 verify, local factory extraction,
local hash, exact match against analyze, slot fit table from the shared
SLOT_GEOMETRY); then the device session driver - prepare, poll for the
physical confirmation (slot taken from the device, never the phone),
session open, sequential chunks with in-place retry and resume from the
device-reported offset after a half-written chunk, finalize, terminal-state
poll. Refuses to touch the device without a token, on protocol mismatch,
when busy, or on confirm timeout.

tests/test_phone_install.mjs pins the module with 18 checks against a mock
device mirroring meta_store_install.c's HTTP contract; registered in
validate.sh --static. Firmware rebuild green (boot-page URL change).

